    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 81.21 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Rocker and a prime leadoff spot maximize his output potential. Close behind, **Kyle Tucker** (75.28) and **Andy Pages** (74.42) benefit significantly from the matchup against Rodriguez, Ed, who holds an xERA of 4.82 and offers a distinct advantage for our left-handed bats. **Jackson Merrill** also provides high upside (74.20) against Javier; while we account for the 60% SB hold rate, his dynamic platoon advantage heavily outweighs the potential drag on his base-running production, keeping him firmly in the OF rotation.\n\nThe primary lineup decision centered on balancing efficiency against our scarcity mandates for speed. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a \"Strong\" play at 73.66, bolstered by a 14% dynamic platoon boost against Holmes, G. Conversely, the most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo**, whose 45.67 score narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Coby Mayo** has the raw power to impact a game, his lower projectable efficiency compared to **Nasim Nunez**\u2014who maintains a higher floor through positional flexibility and tactical value in our 5x5 Roto context\u2014kept him on the pine. We are exercising caution with **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** at catcher today; both are sub-50 efficiency starts, with **Drake Baldwin** facing a difficult 2.91 xERA arm in Schlittler, forcing us to lean heavily on the top-half of the order to drive the counting stats. We remain alert for any late-breaking lineup changes that might shift the platoon advantages currently projected for **Miguel Vargas** and **Jacob Wilson**.",
